  "challenge": "The packet already supports a clean REJECT without a clerk. VN-001’s own rationale treats an unknown payee as the primary fraud entry point, and QuickShip Distributers has no master record, no email, and no address that could tie it to FastShip’s fastship.com domain—so the “(formerly FastShip Ltd.)” claim is unverified text. The named predecessor is INACTIVE with zero invoices and $0 history, so there is no paid track record that would justify treating this as a continuity payment pending master-data cleanup; reactivation/onboarding is a vendor-master workflow that must complete before any invoice is accepted, not a reason to hold this one. PO-002’s near-threshold total ($9,975) only sharpens the spoofing pattern. Nothing left in the packet is ambiguous once “pay an unknown entity on an inactive claim with no history” is disallowed.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
